<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">7 October in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">5 events that happened on 7 October, from 1571 to 3761 BCE.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1571 CE <span class="tih-ago">455 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Holy League defeats the Ottoman fleet at Lepanto</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/galley">Galleys</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-league-1571">Holy League</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-of-austria">Don John of Austria</a> destroyed most of the Ottoman fleet off western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a>. Lepanto was the last great battle of oared galleys and ended the image of Ottoman naval invincibility.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1737 CE <span class="tih-ago">289 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">A cyclone and storm surge devastate Calcutta and Bengal</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A violent cyclone struck the Hooghly delta, wrecking ships and much of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kolkata">Calcutta</a>. Contemporary reports put the dead at 300,000, a figure modern historians consider greatly exaggerated.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bengal">Bengal</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1959 CE <span class="tih-ago">67 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Luna 3 photographs the far side of the Moon</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Soviet probe Luna 3 took the first photographs of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhu">Moon</a>'s far side, which is never visible from Earth. The grainy images revealed a surface with far fewer dark lunar 'seas' than the near side.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/afghanistan" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/afghanistan.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">2001 CE <span class="tih-ago">25 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The US and Britain begin air strikes on Afghanistan</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">American and British forces began bombing Taliban and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-qaeda">al-Qaeda</a> targets in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afghanistan">Afghanistan</a>, four weeks after the 11 September attacks. The war toppled the Taliban but lasted nearly twenty years.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afghanistan">Afghanistan</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">3761 BCE</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The epoch of the Hebrew calendar</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hebrew">Hebrew</a> calendar counts its years from a date equivalent to 7 October 3761 BCE, the traditional date of creation calculated from biblical chronology. Year 1 of this reckoning is still used to number the Jewish year.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hebrew">Hebrew</a></div></div></li></ol>
